    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0913, rpld §11-0913 sub 9, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9462\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to deer\nmanagement permits; and to repeal certain provisions of such law relat-\ning thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:  This bill will authorize the Department of Environmental\nConservation (DEC)to issue deer management permits to the \"Northern\nZone\" of the state to properly manage deer herds, mitigate tick borne\nillnesses, and protect young tree growth.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 paragraph a of subdivision 1 and subdivision 8 of section\n11-0913 of the environmental conservation law is amended such that\nsubparagraph a removes the northern exemption when the additional\nharvest of deer is deemed reasonably necessary to manage to deer herd in\nthe state.\n\nSection 8 removes the exemption of deer management unit thirty-four\nprovision of this section that applies to the \"Northern Zone\" of the\nstate as defined in subdivision sixteen in section 11-0130 is now\nremoved. It is amended to read that the department of environmental\nconservation is authorized and directed to promulgate any rules of regu-\nlation necessary to more particularly describe areas of land set forth\nin the section.\n\nSection 2 repeals subdivision 9 of section 11-0913 of environmental\nconservation law.\n\nSection 3 establishes the immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe \"Northern Zone\" of New York State, which is demarcated by the North-\nern-Southern Hunting Zone line, is experiencing a surge in tick-borne\nillnesses. The Upstate Tick Testing Laboratory has reported a ninefold\nincrease in pathogen-carrying ticks from 2% in 2019 to 18% in 2025, and\ntick activity continues to expand northwards and westward, chiefly via\nthe surplus of deer herds in the state.  This bill intends to mitigate\nthis public health hazard by giving the DEC authority to issue deer\nmanagement permits to hunters in the Northern Zone, which is to be done\nin balance with the available deer range and natural food supply of the\nstate.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2025-26: Introduced.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
